<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory, says new report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb241807f107024ba74b3825f2aa8948b0e8328bc317d645f513c3383d45ef0b</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877--a509ee21abbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a9c40dd754703cd229bef7547028e2825ba7893d4758eaa415a4ea4bd45cd7</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a6a61174d241e9be2370cee6bcba64de1ea54653965ea96e3c4c51802b9b54</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Japan probe sets course for Mars moon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:676f4d68514bd8e0174b63da2305f686bd8bded40a5f74339a112f9f771958b3</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T07:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-probe-sets-course-for-mars-moon/a-79708491--8ca3c6616a26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-probe-sets-course-for-mars-moon/a-79708491?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The MMX spacecraft is on its way to Mars' moon Phobos to collect surface samples that could help answer long-standing questions about the formation of the Solar System.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rubio holds talks with counterpart Jaishankar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36cea3bb45deb317c53840195b71fbc9fc0e135333abff9bd14e49b6e1af3193</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rubio-holds-talks-with-counterpart-jaishankar/live-79708492--c711a58d8b65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rubio-holds-talks-with-counterpart-jaishankar/live-79708492?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Marco Rubio's talks with Indian Foreign Minister Jaishankar come as the two countries struggle to finalize a trade deal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar refugees find hope in Thailand's work program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f5fd316c9435e792a015903c08688e39ead8b329e23ca575e4ef277dcc70625</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921--572ae4634b5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio visits India with a trip to the world's largest oil refinery topping the agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33468319f96b9ff5d9a7d59b303d1df733ce8d48fbeccdaac49aa214dcf7f136</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rubio-visits-india-with-a-trip-to-the-world-s-largest-oil-refinery-topping-the-agenda/a-79699826--dd280f73407c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rubio-visits-india-with-a-trip-to-the-world-s-largest-oil-refinery-topping-the-agenda/a-79699826?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A visit to India this week by Washington's top diplomat will skip New Delhi and instead include the world's largest oil refinery, which processes massive amounts of Russian crude. Is Trump looking for a new deal?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>From delivery driver to global fame: A Korean writer's journey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e1ff8308a0542919b6469c5480929233dc612a4477af50af5480977729a6860</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757--a579002c20b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">You Yeong-Gwang's The Rainfall Market tells the story of a mysterious, hidden shop that only opens when it rains. For a debut novel by an unknown author, it was a massive success.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: CJP alleges 'deliberate' delay in leaders' release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:777b5c0f0be873b4135628a0cc532da191d5325621d865bccb5200329091457e</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cjp-alleges-deliberate-delay-in-leaders-release/live-79695410--74850181e334.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cjp-alleges-deliberate-delay-in-leaders-release/live-79695410?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CJP leaders Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka were due to be released on Sunday. The judge in the case has recused himself after claiming that he was threatened.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The murder of a young mother in Iran has once again sparked debate on femicide and the social acceptance of violence against women.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3395a6f7ae2eb314e43f152300bd809e9220b47361399978557772fa4a1da7b3</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-murder-of-a-young-mother-in-iran-has-once-again-sparked-debate-on-femicide-and-the-social-accept/a-79681977--0dbaaaebbc74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-murder-of-a-young-mother-in-iran-has-once-again-sparked-debate-on-femicide-and-the-social-acceptance-of-violence-against-women/a-79681977?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The murder of a young mother has once again sparked debate in Iran over so-called honor killings, the social acceptance of violence against women and the lack of protection for people vulnerable to gender-based violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f547f8791b1d1018463d56a90efd9b4239bf38826a14bbfb242f057f211f28dc</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0425816692f33c7a0a7519e05a1b190bae9f131963cc8a7093a63f608bc804</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7f6cb5bce7aa02fc3277cd12dcece65f8de19777b343b0a9a88a31a7bc8a45</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual violence cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fueling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
